<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orongo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Orongo is a ceremonial village on the rim of the Rano Kau crater at the south-western tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter-island">Rapa Nui</a> (Easter Island). Its low stone houses and rock carvings of bird men were the centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tangata-manu">Tangata manu</a> cult, in which competitors swam to the islet of Motu Nui to bring back the first sooty tern egg of the season. The rite continued until the 1860s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orongo.jpg" alt="Orongo" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eric Gaba (Sting - fr:Sting) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orongo_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
